-- title:
--   Inertia degree divides the valuation of x after base change
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $L$, $K'$, $M$ be number fields with $K$-algebra structures making $K \subseteq L \subseteq M$ and $K \subseteq K' \subseteq M$ compatible towers, with $L/K$ Galois, $\operatorname{finrank}_{K'} M = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$, and every element of $M$ lying in the $K'$-subalgebra generated by the image of $L$ (so $M$ is the base change $LK'$); assume $n := [L:K]$ is prime and $[K':K] = 2$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ such that every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ whose contraction to $\mathcal{O}_K$ is $v$ has $\mathrm{ramificationIdx}'(v,w) = 1$. Let $\mathfrak{v}$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{K'}$ contracting to $v$, and $\mathfrak{w}$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_M$ contracting to $\mathfrak{v}$. Let $x$ be a nonzero element of the $\mathfrak{v}$-adic completion of $K'$ whose norm over the $v$-adic completion of $K$ has valuation of the form $\exp(n k_0)$ for some $k_0 \in \mathbb{Z}$, the valuations taking values in $\mathbb{Z}^{\mathrm{mult}}$ with zero. The conclusion is that there is $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $\mathrm{Valued.v}\,x = \exp\bigl(\mathrm{inertiaDeg}'(\mathfrak{v},\mathfrak{w}) \cdot k\bigr)$, i.e. the valuation of $x$ lies in $f(\mathfrak{w}\mid\mathfrak{v})\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   A local divisibility step in the descent argument attached to a prime-degree Galois extension and its base change along a quadratic extension: the valuation of a local element whose norm has valuation divisible by $[L:K]$ is itself divisible by the residue degree of $M/K'$ at the chosen places. It is used in the construction of units and tensor factorisations recorded in [`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.exists_units_prod_tensor_map_iterate_eq_tmul_one_of_finrank_dvd_valuation_norm`](thm.html#IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.exists_units_prod_tensor_map_iterate_eq_tmul_one_of_finrank_dvd_valuation_norm).
